    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.user_work_scope.observed_cgroup_bound_tests", decl_name: "NEXT", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.user_work_scope.observed_cgroup_bound_tests", decl_name: "fixture_root", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.user_work_scope.observed_cgroup_bound_tests", decl_name: "tree", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.user_work_scope.observed_cgroup_bound_tests", decl_name: "verdict", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.user_work_scope.observed_cgroup_bound_tests", decl_name: "a_finite_max_with_no_swap_on_the_unit_bounds_it", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.user_work_scope.observed_cgroup_bound_tests", decl_name: "a_limit_on_one_level_and_no_swap_on_another_bounds_the_leaf", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.user_work_scope.observed_cgroup_bound_tests", decl_name: "a_bound_on_an_ancestor_bounds_the_leaf", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.user_work_scope.observed_cgroup_bound_tests", decl_name: "unlimited_max_or_allowed_swap_or_out_of_range_never_bounds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.user_work_scope.observed_cgroup_bound_tests", decl_name: "an_unreadable_chain_or_missing_line_is_unread_not_bounded", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.user_work_scope.standing_fixture_tests", decl_name: "a_system_service_with_an_observed_bound_chain_admits_and_without_one_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
  reason: "The seed trampoline decides whether a gunbc run may proceed unwrapped BEFORE the corpus is resolved, so it cannot evaluate gunbc.compute.unit_bounds user_work_scope_standing and mirrors its arms. The revision job's guest unit runs in an unmodeled system.slice under its own MemoryMax= and MemorySwapMax=0, which main's fold refuses as UncappedSystemSlice; the declared arm that admits it is gunbc.compute.unit_bounds observed_cgroup_bound, reading the process's cgroup chain through extdeps.linux.cgroup_v2_memory. These items are that arm's mirror: the chain walk over /sys/fs/cgroup, its three-valued outcome, the fall-through wire the trampoline prints, and the fixture-tree tests that execute it (including the ordering after the modeled-slice arm and before the system-unit refusal). The mirror is held to the .dag arms by test.claim.live_deploy.user_work_slice_witness the_seed_trampoline_mirrors_the_declared_wrap_standing.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete these items with the rest of cli_run/user_work_scope.rs when the Test/Run wrap is emitted natively from gunbc.compute.unit_bounds, so the standing is evaluated from the .dag fold rather than mirrored. The .dag witness's bounded, unbounded and unread rows must remain enrolled; removing them is not dissolution.",
  current_boundary: "gunbc run -> v1_compiler.cli_run.user_work_scope reexec_into_user_work_slice_if_owed -> standing_from_supplied -> observed_cgroup_bound -> /proc/self/cgroup and memory.max and memory.swap.max under /sys/fs/cgroup/<chain>"
}
